Show that if $u(x, y)$ is harmonic on the entire plane $RR^2$ and bounded from above by a real constant $M$ ($u(x, y) <= M$), then $u$ must be:

#pagebreak()
#set page(width: a_width, margin: a_margin)
#set text(size: a_size)
Identically constant

#pagebreak()
#set page(width: a_width, margin: a_margin)
#set text(size: a_size)
Strictly negative everywhere

#pagebreak()
#set page(width: a_width, margin: a_margin)
#set text(size: a_size)
A linear function $a x + b y + c$

#pagebreak()
#set page(width: a_width, margin: a_margin)
#set text(size: a_size)
Bounded from below by $-M$

